  <prompt>Fix the three confirmed Bicep source-vs-code config drifts before ANY stamp redeploy (DS-5 ordering rule: 'C5.1+C5.2 source fixes FIRST -- they must be in the template before ANY stamp redeploy, or the redeploy wipes the live aliases and bricks the running service'). C5.1: modules/controlplane-app-service.bicep:114-145 emits Cosmos__Endpoint/Cosmos__Database/Cosmos__RunsContainer but the code reads Cosmos:AccountEndpoint (CosmosModule.cs:98) / Cosmos:DatabaseName (:110) / Cosmos:ContainerName -- rename the emitted keys; replace ServiceBus__ConnectionString (KV ref) with ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace={sbNamespace}.servicebus.windows.net + ServiceBus__QueueName=sprk-provisioning-jobs (ServiceBusModule.cs:53 documents the connection string is IGNORED, MI-only); add ManagedIdentity__ClientId=uamiClientId (keep AZURE_CLIENT_ID too, DefaultAzureCredential honors it natively); remove the now-dead serviceBusKeyVaultSecretName param + servicebus-connection-string secret plumbing (platform-controlplane.bicep:101). C5.2: platform-controlplane.bicep:151 jwtAudience var -- change 'api://spaarke-provisioning-controlplane-${environmentName}' to 'api://spaarke.com/provisioning-controlplane-${environmentName}' (tenant-policy-forced verifier-domain form; matches the already-corrected SKILL.md). C5.3: dataverseClientSecretName param (platform-controlplane.bicep:104-105 + controlplane-app-service.bicep:137-141) -- mark @description deprecated-pending-C1.4 for now (task 111/112 remove it once Path X lands); keep the dummy KV binding until then.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Bicep appSettings array semantics (full-replace on redeploy) and config-key contract verification against .NET IOptions binding sections.</role>

  <goal>modules/controlplane-app-service.bicep emits Cosmos__AccountEndpoint, Cosmos__DatabaseName, Cosmos__ContainerName, ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace, ServiceBus__QueueName, ManagedIdentity__ClientId (alongside AZURE_CLIENT_ID) -- matching every key CosmosModule.cs/ServiceBusModule.cs actually reads. platform-controlplane.bicep's jwtAudience is api://spaarke.com/provisioning-controlplane-{env}. The dead serviceBusKeyVaultSecretName param + KV secret plumbing is removed. dataverseClientSecretName param carries a deprecated-pending-C1.4 description. az bicep build succeeds; a what-if against dev shows the app-setting diff matches exactly this key-rename set with no unintended changes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-5's Category-5 table (grep-verified against platform-controlplane.bicep + modules/controlplane-app-service.bicep + modules/service-bus.bicep) found ZERO Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments resources in platform-controlplane.bicep (only a comment describing intended grants) and confirmed the appSettings array fully replaces live settings on every `az deployment` -- meaning every live manual alias the dev stamp currently relies on dies on the next redeploy unless the SOURCE template is fixed first. This is DS-5's #1 ordering rule for the whole Cat-5 remediation set.</background>
