  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- the live dev stamp currently works ONLY because someone manually aliased the app settings after a Bicep deploy that emitted the wrong keys; the source template itself is broken. Extension -- there is no existing-correct template to extend; the fix IS the extension, applied directly to the two Bicep files that own these emissions. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- the very next `az deployment` (needed by tasks 101, 108, 110 to add new resources) would silently wipe the live manual aliases and take Cosmos/SB connectivity down with it -- a self-inflicted outage during THIS wave's own work.

COMPLETION (2026-08-19): All C5.1-C5.3 fixes landed source-side. C5.1: renamed Cosmos__Endpoint/__Database/__RunsContainer -> Cosmos__AccountEndpoint/__DatabaseName/__ContainerName; replaced ServiceBus__ConnectionString KV-ref with ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace ({ns}.servicebus.windows.net, built from a new serviceBusNamespaceName param) + ServiceBus__QueueName (new serviceBusQueueName param, default sprk-provisioning-jobs); added ManagedIdentity__ClientId alongside AZURE_CLIENT_ID. C5.2: jwtAudience -> api://spaarke.com/provisioning-controlplane-{env} in platform-controlplane.bicep + comment/description text in both files. C5.3: dataverseClientSecretName @description marked deprecated-pending-C1.4 in both files; dummy KV binding retained unchanged. Also fixed stacks/dev.bicepparam:12 B1->P1v3 (auth-v4 §8 item 4).

Deviation from POML step 6 (Path C, directed by orchestrator, not improvised): orchestrator instructions explicitly said "Do NOT execute Bicep against live Azure. Authoring + az bicep build validation only" -- the `az deployment sub what-if` verification step + its acceptance criterion were NOT run against live dev for deploy-safety reasons. `az bicep build` passed clean (exit 0) on both files after regen. What-if verification is deferred to whoever runs the next live deploy (task 113's Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 or an operator-run what-if) -- flagging so it is not silently skipped.

Additive on top of tasks 108 (queue module) and 101 (worker app service + platform-controlplane wiring) -- verified via grep before editing; zero conflicts, all task 108/101 content preserved.

Fix-drift-at-discovery items surfaced (not fixed in this task, out of scope):
1. `modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` (authored by task 101, AFTER DS-5 was written) carries the IDENTICAL C5.1 key-shape drift (Cosmos__Endpoint/__Database/__RunsContainer + ServiceBus__ConnectionString KV-ref) -- DS-5's C5.1 table only scoped the .Api module because the .Worker module didn't exist yet when DS-5 was authored. Recommend a small follow-on task applying the same rename to the Worker module before its first live deploy runs handlers against real Cosmos/SB.
2. `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-app-service.json` + `infrastructure/bicep/platform-controlplane.json` (compiled ARM JSON, tracked in git) were STALE -- last regenerated at task 033 (original authoring commit d3b994434), never regenerated by tasks 101 or 108 despite both modifying the .bicep source. Regenerated both via `az bicep build --outfile` as part of this task's validation pass; the resulting diff (546 lines in platform-controlplane.json) reflects catching up 2 prior tasks' worth of source drift, not new content from this task. Recommend teams running `az bicep build --outfile` as a standard last step whenever touching a .bicep file that has a tracked compiled .json sibling.
